{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"cross_transformation","type":"text","text":"**Every arrow in the signal chain is a transformation.**\nNot a pipe that carries data intact — a site where something is amplified and something is reduced. The impasse often lives at exactly one of these arrows. Which one is yours?","x":-200,"y":-1780,"width":380,"height":180,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cross_labor","type":"text","text":"**The matter-network requires maintenance.**\nWhen it breaks, you find out what it actually is. The impasse is not a failure of the network — it is the network becoming visible. This is often the most honest view of your project you will have all term.","x":-200,"y":-1520,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"dq1","type":"text","text":"Where in your project has *becoming digital* created a new object? What did you gain? What is no longer there?","x":-1040,"y":-1220,"width":340,"height":100,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq2","type":"text","text":"What is the script of your primary tool? What does it assume you want to do, and are you working with that assumption or against it?","x":-640,"y":-1220,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq3","type":"text","text":"Name every element in your matter-network right now. Which connections are stable? Which are fragile? Where is the maintenance labor concentrated?","x":-220,"y":-1220,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq4","type":"text","text":"What keeps breaking in your project at the same point(s)? What assumption is that recurring friction disconfirming?","x":200,"y":-1220,"width":340,"height":100,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dq5","type":"text","text":"If your impasse is actually a signal, what is it signaling? What does it want you to notice about your project that you couldn't see before you got here?","x":620,"y":-1220,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"studio","type":"text","text":"### Studio Time — Deep Making Begins\n*The rest of the session.*\n\nYou are not prototyping anymore. You are making.\n\nBring your matter-network into contact with itself. Follow what resists. When you hit an impasse, write it down before you try to fix it. The journal entry is due before next session.","x":-200,"y":-900,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"journal_note","type":"text","text":"> [!note] Journal Entry 2 — First Impasse Report\n> Due before Week 07.\n> Not a problem report. A site of inquiry.\n> Name the impasse. Name the disconfirmed assumption. Name what becomes possible now.","x":380,"y":-860,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"imp_hassle","type":"text","text":"**The Hassle (Agre)**\nNot a one-off bug — a recurring friction. Something that keeps happening at the same point, for reasons you can't quite name. Hassles are structural. They mark the gap between how the tool models the world and how the world actually works.","x":240,"y":-2200,"width":300,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# Week 05 — Enact Thought\n*Deep making begins. Closing Camus & Vinck. Meeting your first impasse.*","x":-280,"y":-2720,"width":660,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cv_thickness","type":"text","text":"**Thickness of Digital Objects**\nDigital objects break, resist, require maintenance, behave differently across versions and environments. The fiction of frictionless digital experience hides enormous labor and loss.","x":-840,"y":-2160,"width":300,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cv_becoming","type":"text","text":"**Becoming Digital**\nMoving something into a digital system is not copying it, it is creating a new object. Something is gained. Something is irretrievably lost. The two objects are not the same thing in two formats.","x":-1320,"y":-2240,"width":300,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cv_anchor","type":"text","text":"## Camus + Vinck\n*Unfolding Digital Materiality*","x":-560,"y":-2440,"width":300,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"thread_Failure_as_Method","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Threads/Failure as Method.md","x":-400,"y":-400,"width":280,"height":440,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"thread_Physical_Digital_Entanglement","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Threads/Physical-Digital Entanglement.md","x":-60,"y":-400,"width":280,"height":440,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"thread_Enabling_Constraints","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Threads/Enabling Constraints.md","x":280,"y":-400,"width":280,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"thread_Entanglement","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Threads/Entanglement.md","x":-740,"y":-400,"width":280,"height":400,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"thread_Research_Creation","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Threads/Research-Creation.md","x":-1080,"y":-400,"width":280,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"warmup","type":"text","text":"### The Paper Exercise\n*~25 minutes — before anything else*\n\nOne sheet of paper. Three rounds: flat, folded, crumpled.\n\nFor each state: *What does it respond to? What would change it?* Then: *If this were an instrument, what would it measure or express?*\n\nWe are not warming up. We are practicing the disposition.","x":-1040,"y":-3080,"width":380,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"imp_assumption","type":"text","text":"**The Disconfirmed Assumption**\nBehind every impasse is something you were treating as settled that isn't. A material behavior. A tool's capability. A protocol's reliability. Naming the assumption is more useful than fixing the symptom.","x":680,"y":-1800,"width":300,"height":220,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"imp_signal","type":"text","text":"**Impasse as Signal**\nAn impasse is not evidence that the project has failed. It is data about the project's structure — something the work couldn't have revealed without getting this far. The question is not *how do I fix this* but *what is this telling me?*","x":740,"y":-2200,"width":300,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cv_script","type":"text","text":"**Scripts + Inscriptions**\nEvery tool encodes a theory of use: valid inputs, valid operations, valid outputs. To use a tool is to partially accept its worldview. Critical practice means knowing when you're complying and when you're pushing back.","x":-400,"y":-2200,"width":300,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"subA","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 05 - Enact Thought/submodules/DIGM 553 - W05A - Matter-Networks and Becoming Digital.md","x":-1700,"y":-1400,"width":500,"height":560,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cv_network","type":"text","text":"**Matter-Network**\nThe project is not a thing — it is a set of relations between things, maintained through active labor. Sensor, cable, library, code, body, environment: none of these alone *is* the project. The project lives in the connections.","x":-1180,"y":-1820,"width":300,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"impasse_anchor","type":"text","text":"## First Impasse\n*Failure as method, enacted*","x":300,"y":-2420,"width":300,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"subB","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 05 - Enact Thought/submodules/DIGM 553 - W05B - First Impasse.md","x":1080,"y":-1400,"width":500,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"quote_cv","type":"text","text":"> [!quote] 'Digital objects are not immaterial — they are *differently material*. They have texture, weight, agency, and resistance. To ignore this is to misunderstand the medium.'\n> — Camus & Vinck, *Unfolding Digital Materiality*","x":-1180,"y":-2620,"width":460,"height":200},
		{"id":"0f930ab9aac25ca5","x":-200,"y":-3380,"width":680,"height":400,"type":"link","url":"https://vimeo.com/1187363445?fl=ml&fe=ec"},
		{"id":"quote_agre","type":"text","text":"> [!quote] 'The goal is not to eliminate the hassle but to understand it — to treat it as information about the structure of the system and the assumptions built into it.'\n> — Agre, *Critical Technical Practice*","x":740,"y":-2520,"width":460,"height":200},
		{"id":"03ba8482f0a92cef","x":700,"y":-3040,"width":740,"height":400,"type":"link","url":"https://vimeo.com/1187363721?fl=ml&fe=ec"}
	],
